WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.086 --> 00:00:07.336
Ally dropped down on a park bench.

2
00:00:07.337 --> 00:00:11.252
"I shouldn't have told Kate that I lost my phone," Ally thought.

3
00:00:11.253 --> 00:00:14.911
"That was a big lie—and a big mistake!"

4
00:00:14.912 --> 00:00:18.257
But Ally hadn't known what else to do.

5
00:00:18.258 --> 00:00:21.334
She couldn't let Kate find out the truth about Alpha.

6
00:00:21.335 --> 00:00:23.570
It was too dangerous.

7
00:00:23.571 --> 00:00:29.506
"I know," she thought. "I'll leave Alpha home until I blast off with Lainie.

8
00:00:29.507 --> 00:00:37.222
And then, when it's time to go, I'll pretend I found the phone—and give it to Kate as my going-away present!" Happy

9
00:00:37.223 --> 00:00:44.424
she'd come up with a good plan, Ally hurried home. She

10
00:00:44.425 --> 00:00:48.459
went to her room and turned Alpha back on. "Alpha,

11
00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:54.688
I have to tell you my great idea for a going-away gift for Mateo," she said. "I'm

12
00:00:54.689 --> 00:01:02.417
going to throw a party, so we can celebrate all of the Earthlings' Holly Days at once, before we leave. Except

13
00:01:02.418 --> 00:01:05.183
I don't know what they are. Can

14
00:01:05.184 --> 00:01:12.297
you look up Holly Days ? They sound a bit like Astral Days on Astralia."

15
00:01:12.298 --> 00:01:18.573
"Affirmative." The old phone hummed and buzzed as Alpha worked to get the information.

16
00:01:18.574 --> 00:01:21.569
"I located a record for holly

17
00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:24.839
. It is a plant with spiky leaves and red berries.

18
00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.161
It is a traditional Christmas decoration," Alpha said.

19
00:01:29.162 --> 00:01:32.656
"Interesting. But what's Christmas?"

20
00:01:32.657 --> 00:01:40.520
Alpha buzzed again. "Christmas is a religious holiday celebrated mainly by Christian Earthlings in December.

21
00:01:40.521 --> 00:01:44.939
Hannukah is celebrated by Jewish Earthlings around the same time.

22
00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:52.074
And Kwanzaa is a celebration of life and African heritage, also celebrated in December."

23
00:01:52.075 --> 00:01:56.662
"Are there any other Holly Days I should know about?" Ally asked.

24
00:01:56.663 --> 00:01:59.980
"In November some Earthlings celebrate Thanksgiving.

25
00:01:59.981 --> 00:02:06.188
Valentine's Day is celebrated in February, and Lunar New Year is in January or February.

26
00:02:06.189 --> 00:02:09.301
Passover and Easter are in the spring."

27
00:02:09.302 --> 00:02:13.826
"Earthlings have so many Holly Days!" Ally exclaimed.

28
00:02:13.827 --> 00:02:18.216
"Alpha, please make a list of foods people eat on Holly Days."

29
00:02:18.217 --> 00:02:22.756
"Affirmative." A few minutes later, Alpha reported back.

30
00:02:22.757 --> 00:02:30.454
"People eat turkey and stuffing for Thanksgiving . . ." Alpha made a strange, loud, crackling noise.

31
00:02:30.455 --> 00:02:34.478
Ally looked up. "Are you okay?"

32
00:02:34.479 --> 00:02:39.890
"I'm fine." Alpha went back to reporting the information about foods.

33
00:02:39.891 --> 00:02:42.905
"They give red chocolate hearts on Christmas.

34
00:02:42.906 --> 00:02:50.074
They paint eggs for Valentine's Day, and chocolate sauce is poured on the Thanksgiving turkey."

35
00:02:50.075 --> 00:02:53.580
"Everything sounds so fun!" Ally said.

36
00:02:53.581 --> 00:02:58.175
"This is going to be the perfect going-away present for Mateo.

37
00:02:58.176 --> 00:03:01.268
Can you please make a shopping list for me?"

38
00:03:01.269 --> 00:03:04.006
"Preparing it now," Alpha said.

39
00:03:04.007 --> 00:03:08.249
"Thanks. Now I just have to figure out when to have the party.

40
00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.699
It has to be before I leave with Lainie Polk."

41
00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.763
"T-minus two weeks to blastoff," Alpha said.

42
00:03:15.764 --> 00:03:20.730
"Whoa! That's soon!" Ally suddenly realized something.

43
00:03:20.731 --> 00:03:25.327
"I haven't heard from Lainie lately. Have I missed any calls from her?"

44
00:03:25.328 --> 00:03:30.339
"Negative. Last incoming communication was exactly 13 days ago."

45
00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:36.614
"That's odd. Let's call her," Ally said.

46
00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:41.984
Lainie's assistant answered the phone. "Sorry, Ally, but Lainie is out of the office."

47
00:03:41.985 --> 00:03:46.096
"Okay, can you ask her to call me back?" Ally asked.

48
00:03:46.097 --> 00:03:49.345
"I'm afraid she's out of the country without any cell service.

49
00:03:49.346 --> 00:03:51.510
I'll have her call you when she returns."

50
00:03:51.511 --> 00:03:54.483
"Thank you." Ally hung up.

51
00:03:54.484 --> 00:03:57.710
"Reply does not compute," Alpha said.

52
00:03:57.711 --> 00:04:03.177
"Sure, it does." Silly Alpha—she was acting up again.

53
00:04:03.178 --> 00:04:05.835
"Lainie will call me as soon as she's back.

54
00:04:05.836 --> 00:04:09.235
But, Alpha, I need you to stay quiet today.

55
00:04:09.236 --> 00:04:17.886
Don't make any noise at all, except for text messages and when Lainie calls. Understand?"

56
00:04:17.887 --> 00:04:20.491
"Hmpf!" Alpha made a snorting noise. "I

57
00:04:20.492 --> 00:04:27.389
understand loud and clear!" The screen turned black as Alpha went into Sleep mode. ***

58
00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:31.459
Later Ally walked back into town to meet Mateo at the print shop.

59
00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:34.880
She brought Alpha because she was still waiting for Lainie's call.

60
00:04:34.881 --> 00:04:39.780
As she walked along, she noticed flyers posted everywhere.

61
00:04:39.781 --> 00:04:45.317
She stopped to read one: "Lost Phone! Reward for Its Safe Return."

62
00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:49.594
"That's sad," Ally thought. "Someone lost their phone."

63
00:04:49.595 --> 00:04:53.677
But then Ally looked closer and saw the photo on the flyers.

64
00:04:53.678 --> 00:04:57.241
It was a picture of Ally with Alpha in her hand.

65
00:04:57.242 --> 00:05:06.093
"Oh no!" Ally groaned. "Now people all over town will be looking for my phone—and me!

66
00:05:06.094 --> 00:05:08.535
I should have left Alpha at home!"

67
00:05:08.536 --> 00:05:13.363
Just then Alpha buzzed with a text message. It was from Kate:

68
00:05:13.364 --> 00:05:18.194
I'll have final T-shirt designs for you later today.

69
00:05:18.195 --> 00:05:22.994
"Alpha, write back and say, 'Thanks for . . .'" Ally remembered something.

70
00:05:22.995 --> 00:05:28.563
"Wait! Never mind! I told Kate I lost my phone, so I can't reply.

71
00:05:28.564 --> 00:05:34.087
Instead I have to pretend I didn't see the text. Ugh!" Ally groaned.

72
00:05:34.088 --> 00:05:41.493
"Life is so much easier on Astralia, where we can read one another's minds!"

